   00167| /// Whether the code catalog itself can template `task` into a written program.
   00168| ///
   00169| /// The open-web decision table asks this before answering a bare term at the
   00170| /// end of its cascade: a request the catalog can write is a coding request,
   00171| /// and the coding routes -- not a web search -- speak for it (issue #907). The
   00172| /// boundary is the catalog, not an output literal, because the typed recipe
   00173| /// path also composes programs no contract pins.
   00174| pub(super) fn catalog_claims(task: &str) -> bool {
   00175|     generated_artifact(task).is_some()
